From 45057a110dc69ba5dfae8ab78c76810419d161ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MCShotty <108978104+MCShotty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 04:16:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/20] feat(video): add 8K presets and camera frame-rate
 controls

Offer resolution presets through 7680x4320 for camera and screen sharing,
and saved 15/30/60 fps camera controls on both video backends. Thread the
selected dimensions and rate through native capture, encoding and signaling.

Bound native buffers by negotiated geometry, retain small UI previews and
scale encoded-picture budgets only for larger presets. Use jitter-tolerant
camera cadence, elapsed-time RTP pacing and an independent bounded async
camera receive path so the audio tick does not cap delivery at 50 fps.

Record offline native screenshots, source-backed regression checks and
scoped performance observations; disclose unavailable full desktop/package
and physical 8K hardware validation.
